  "title": "Al-Razi (Rhazes)",
  "summary": "Al-Razi, born in Rayy in about 865, was a physician who headed hospitals in Rayy and Baghdad and served at the Samanid court. His medical writings include the Book of Medicine for Mansur and a treatise on smallpox and measles dated c. 922, which one source calls the first clinical account of smallpox. He died at Rayy about 925.",
